  "note": "Regional invasive-species lists, used to earn the Invasive label and the ring on the map. 'Introduced' (iNaturalist establishment means) is not 'invasive' (a policy determination by an authority), and this file holds only the second. scope names the jurisdiction whose list an entry comes from, habitat says whether the species belongs to Riffle's freshwater and riparian scope, and why states the One Health relevance in plain language. The European Union entries are the aquatic and riparian species of Union concern under Regulation (EU) 1143/2014, plus a few species that are not Union-listed but dominate European urban freshwater and are labelled as such in source. The California entries are inherited from SpeciesGuard, the terrestrial project Riffle grew out of, and are kept so existing users keep their answers. scientific_name is the name iNaturalist currently accepts; synonyms hold the older names lists and vision models still use, and matching checks both. Every entry must be re-verified against the cited authority before it is used for anything beyond screening and map highlighting.",
